Adapted source: scripts/lib/process.mjs (commit
501f975372ddb5117b6389114c15f1ccd0104711) was adapted, with modifications, into
src/adapters/process-spawn.ts of this project. Modifications include the
TypeScript ESM rewrite, injection-friendly types for this project's frozen
adapter contract, and additional termination verification. The adapted file
carries an attribution header.

The upstream project's NOTICE is reproduced below as required.

This product also includes adapted software from the zcode-acp project
(https://github.com/william0wang/zcode-acp), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.

Adapted source: src/tasks-index.ts was adapted, with modifications, into
src/adapters/task-index-sync.ts. Modifications include Bridge task correlation,
custom ZCODE_HOME path resolution, runtime schema checks, preserving Desktop-
owned rows and titles, and best-effort session status synchronization.

This product also includes software adapted from the public ZCode source at
commit aac4755666d09fdcd70272fcf063c077a639015f (Apache-2.0), used to implement
the optional Bridge browser host (ADR-007):

  Adapted sources: packages/shared/src/browser-use/{command-metadata,commands,
  backend,result,snapshot}.ts were adapted, with modifications, into
  src/browser/{command-metadata,commands,backend,result,snapshot-schema}.ts.
  Modifications keep the official interaction/browserList and
  interaction/browserExecute wire schemas while consolidating the shared
  package into this repository's module layout and making host-side request
  parsing tolerant of advisory-field drift.

  Adapted sources: apps/zcode-cli/packages/adapters/src/browser/{index,session,
  page-command,playwright-command,snapshot,request,descriptor,executable}.ts
  were adapted, with modifications, into src/browser/{runtime,session,
  page-command,playwright-command,snapshot-capture,request,descriptor,
  executable}.ts. Modifications replace @zcode/contracts imports with local
  modules, bind the browser lifecycle to a Bridge task attempt, report
  unverified teardowns honestly (connection-state verdicts, late-launch
  recycling), and rewrite error text for Bridge runtime settings.

  Adapted source: apps/zcode-cli/packages/contracts/src/interfaces/
  browser-control.port.ts was adapted, with modifications, into
  src/browser/contracts.ts. Modifications drop TraceContext and child-session
  derivation: the Bridge host binds every request to the single active task
  session and registers no child sessions.

Each adapted file carries an attribution header and in-place annotations for
Bridge-specific changes.

This product also includes a thin task-waiter lifecycle adapted from PR #49 of
codex-zcode-bridge (head 13ab83626a7fa7f35319a21244215c2915ecb112), contributed
by Bill <chen.pengyu1@student.zy.cdut.edu.cn>, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. The adapted source retains argument validation, bounded waiting,
polling, bounded JSON output, exit-code handling, and the read-only host
lifecycle. Its task-state observation was replaced with the shared SQLite
Attention Core; legacy event-tail parsing, request-ID pairing, and JSON task
files were removed. The adapted file carries an attribution header.

